      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/romney_indiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Monon Railroad, chartered as New Albany and Salem in 1847, brought vital transport for crops, shaping Romney's growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/romney_indiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1842, marking Romney's early establishment and serving as a community hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romney%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Romney lies about 12 miles north of the Wabash River, whose valley affects local drainage.",
